# Rust build artifacts
target/
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.bak

# Per-developer Cargo config — used to override target-dir, registry,
# linker, etc. for a single checkout without affecting CI or other
# contributors. Common use case: relocate target/ to a different drive
# via `[build] target-dir = "D:/somewhere"` so debug build artifacts
# (which can grow to ~100 GB) don't sit on the system drive.
.cargo/

# IDE / editor
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Solo runtime files (should never be checked in)
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
hnsw_*.bin
hnsw_*.bin.tmp
hnsw_*.bin.bak
solo.db*
solo-data/

# Logs
*.log
logs/

# Local config / secrets
.env
.env.local
*.pem
*.key
*.cdx.json

# Test artifacts
coverage/
*.profraw
*.profdata
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.dev-session/
.smoke/

# Generated Windows release artifacts
installer/windows/SoloSetup-*.exe
installer/windows/SoloSetup-*.zip
installer/windows/soloLatest.zip

# v0.9.0 P3: fastembed-rs's hf-hub model cache. fastembed downloads
# all-MiniLM-L6-v2 weights (~22 MB) on first use and caches them
# under `.fastembed_cache/` (in CWD) when running tests. The cache is
# transient build state — keep it out of git history.
.fastembed_cache/
**/.fastembed_cache/
